WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:12.050
Most of what makes an official effective happens in the details of a meeting: how you read the packet, what you ask, how you make a motion, and how you handle a hard room.

2
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.292
Torrance has its own rules of order.

3
00:00:14.292 --> 00:00:22.140
It does not use Robert's Rules or Rosenberg's Rules, though most neighboring cities use Rosenberg's, so it helps to know both.

4
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.067
Read a staff report in this order.

5
00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:28.318
Start with the recommendation and the findings you are being asked to make.

6
00:00:28.318 --> 00:00:33.532
Then check which law governs the item, and whether state housing law limits your discretion.

7
00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:36.649
Next, the environmental determination and its evidence.

8
00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:42.317
Then the conditions of approval: do they connect to the project's impacts, and can they be enforced?

9
00:00:42.317 --> 00:00:45.604
Then the plan policies staff cites, and any it leaves out.

10
00:00:45.604 --> 00:00:49.515
Then public letters, especially factual claims staff hasn't answered.

11
00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:52.122
Then the alternatives staff did not recommend.

12
00:00:52.122 --> 00:00:57.280
And finally, the deadlines, including how many of the five housing hearings have been used.

13
00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.183
Ask questions that build the record, not speeches.

14
00:01:00.183 --> 00:01:02.273
What evidence supports finding four?

15
00:01:02.273 --> 00:01:05.930
is a better question than saying you are worried about traffic.

16
00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:11.039
Send detailed technical questions to staff a day or two ahead, so the answers are ready.

17
00:01:11.039 --> 00:01:15.045
Ask staff to respond on the record to factual claims from the public.

18
00:01:15.045 --> 00:01:19.573
Ask the applicant whether they would accept a condition before you propose it.

19
00:01:19.573 --> 00:01:24.740
And ask the city attorney, in public, what your discretion is when a state law may apply.

20
00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:30.995
A good land use motion has three parts: the environmental action, the decision, and the findings and conditions.

21
00:01:30.995 --> 00:01:46.353
For example: I move to find the project exempt under the infill exemption, and to approve the use permit based on the findings in the staff report, with finding six modified as discussed, subject to the conditions in the exhibit, with a new condition limiting delivery hours.

22
00:01:46.353 --> 00:01:58.360
Under Torrance's council rules, a motion needs a second, only one substitute motion may be pending at a time, a tie fails, and reconsideration may be moved only by a member on the winning side or one who was absent.

23
00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:09.020
If you chair, keep the same sequence every time: the staff report, clarifying questions, the applicant, public comment, rebuttal, close the hearing, deliberation, motion, and vote.

24
00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:12.396
Speak last, and make a motion only when no one else will.

25
00:02:12.396 --> 00:02:17.370
Restate the motion before the vote, and announce the result, including who voted no.

26
00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:21.042
When a room turns hostile, the law gives you tools and limits.

27
00:02:21.042 --> 00:02:27.912
You must first warn a disruptive person that continuing may lead to removal, and may remove them if they don't stop.

28
00:02:27.912 --> 00:02:33.183
If a group makes the meeting impossible, the room can be cleared, but the press may stay.

29
00:02:33.183 --> 00:02:36.321
You may not, however, prohibit criticism of the body.

30
00:02:36.321 --> 00:02:48.580
The craft is mostly prevention: explain the process and the legal limits at the start, apply time limits equally to every side, call a short recess before tempers break, and thank even the angriest speakers.

31
00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:51.619
Deliberate out loud on the findings, not your preferences.

32
00:02:51.619 --> 00:02:56.021
Say which findings you can make and which you can't, and point to specific evidence.

33
00:02:56.021 --> 00:03:02.675
If the discussion reveals missing information, continue the item with specific direction rather than deciding on a thin record.

34
00:03:02.675 --> 00:03:06.500
For more, see the meeting craft section of the Local Official's Handbook.
